# Prompt Arena: Mystery — environment.
#
# The deployment (Vercel) needs:
#   SESSION_SECRET   signs session cookies (required in production)
#   DATABASE_URL     Postgres connection string (Vercel Postgres / Neon).
#                    Without it requests fall back to a per-instance /tmp
#                    SQLite file, which only suits a demo.
#
# Optional:
#   EVENT_MODE=true            disables practice starts, chapter selection and
#                              the accusation shortcut, enables the event
#                              leaderboard + timing rules (sign-in stays open:
#                              guest names and Google both mark the team entered)
#   ADMIN_USERNAME / ADMIN_PASSWORD   the /admin/ control room (required in
#                              production; local development uses admin/arena-admin)
#   DEV_TEAM_CODE              seeds the developer sandbox team, opened with
#                              POST /api/dev/login (see docs/DEVTOOLS.md);
#                              unset and the sandbox does not exist
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET             Google sign-in (offered
#                              on the login screen when set; a guest name is
#                              always offered)
#   GOOGLE_AUTH_URL / GOOGLE_TOKEN_URL / GOOGLE_USERINFO_URL   (override URLs)
#
# Live AI suspects: every character answers from the Console free tier, with
# deepseek-v4.1-flash-free as the primary model — no paid endpoint involved.
# Secrets: set these in the host env, never in repo.
#   OPENCODE_API_KEY=k       a free-tier Console key. Requests run on the
#                          opencode.ai/inference/v1 chat endpoint; usage limits
#                          and errors fail over across the free model pool.
#   LLM_MODELS=deepseek-v4.1-flash-free   the default already; list more of the
#                          free models (big-pickle, mimo-v2.6-flash-free, ...)
#                          to widen the failover pool.
#   LLM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=320     reply budget per call.
#   LLM_FIRST_TOKEN_MS=9000 / LLM_TURN_BUDGET_MS=22000 / LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT=32
#                          pool timing and concurrency for 100 teams.
#   LLM_MAX_ATTEMPTS=16 / LLM_COOLDOWN_MS=60000 / LLM_MAX_COOLDOWN_MS=900000
# Abuse guards, all server-side: one live interview per team at a time, a 1.5s
# minimum between questions, 12 questions/minute per team, and
# LLM_TEAM_DAILY_MAX=500 model answers per team per day. Past any guard the
# authored answers still reply — no team is ever left without a response, and
# the pooled usage is protected.
#
# Local development (`npm run dev:game`) works without any of these: it binds
# 127.0.0.1, signs guests in instantly, and stores progress in .game-dev.local.

SESSION_SECRET=change-me
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/db
# EVENT_MODE=false
# DEV_TEAM_CODE=DEV-ARENA
